From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Mitchell <me@gmitch215.xyz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:50:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: leave cache-aware scheduling off

Linux 7.3 adds CONFIG_SCHED_CACHE, on by default for SMP kernels. It
steers the tasks of one process onto one last-level cache domain, and
it allocates per-CPU accounting for every new mm_struct. The port runs
every CPU on one host thread, so there is no cache to aggregate on and
nothing for the option to decide, but each exec still pays for the
allocation.

The same 7.3 source built for x86-64 and booted under QEMU, 30 boots per
arm, shows it on an exec that fails with ENOEXEC (the one failing exec
that reaches alloc_bprm): 15.0% to 18.6% slower with the option on, and
0.9% slower to 0.4% faster with it off, against 7.0.14. On the wasm
kernel the same exec is 33.5% slower with the option on and 9.6% slower
with it off (30 rounds; 31.0% and 9.5% pooled with a second window), so
the option accounts for about 21 points of the 31. Reading the source
puts the cost in mm_init(); it was not profiled. Serving does not move
with the option beyond the run-to-run noise.

The defconfig now says the option is off.
---
 arch/wasm/configs/wasm32_nommu_defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/wasm/configs/wasm32_nommu_defconfig b/arch/wasm/configs/wasm32_nommu_defconfig
index 60444d971d..9b17b45920 100644
--- a/arch/wasm/configs/wasm32_nommu_defconfig
+++ b/arch/wasm/configs/wasm32_nommu_defconfig
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 # CONFIG_LOCALVERSION_AUTO is not set
 CONFIG_NO_HZ_FULL=y
+# CONFIG_SCHED_CACHE is not set
 CONFIG_BLK_DEV_INITRD=y
 CONFIG_EXPERT=y
 # CONFIG_IO_URING is not set
-- 
2.43.0

